We are asked to compute the matrix multiplication
$$\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 \\ 4 & 8 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$$
We perform the matrix multiplication as follows:
$$ \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 \\ 4 & 8 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} (1)(5) + (2)(3) \\ (4)(5) + (8)(3) \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 5 + 6 \\ 20 + 24 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 11 \\ 44 \end{pmatrix} $$

\boxed{ \begin{pmatrix} 11 \\ 44 \end{pmatrix} }

\boxed{11}

