However, Pierre, Rosa, and Thomas can sit in different orders within their group. There are $3! = 3 \times 2 \times 1 = 6$ ways to arrange them.

So, the total number of ways to seat the 8 people around the round table with Pierre, Rosa, and Thomas sitting together is $5! \times 3! = 120 \times 6 = 720$.

\boxed{720}

